issue.description:
Add Prometheus alerts on athena that would have caught the 2026-10-17 Plex compromise within minutes instead of ~5 hours:

- sustained CPU (>2 cores for 10m) by service accounts (`plex`, `debian-transmission`, `prometheus`, ...) — needs a per-user/process metric source (process-exporter or a node_exporter textfile collector), since node_exporter alone only shows host load (load average sat near 70 from ~02:15 to ~07:00 unnoticed);
- any process executing from `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, `/dev/shm`, or a deleted binary;
- outbound TCP to common mining-pool ports (3333/4444/5555/14444) — e.g. an nft counter exported via textfile;
- route alerts to a channel Bryan actually sees (Telegram/email).

Evidence: research:202610/athena_plex_compromise_incident_report.md ("Preventing a repeat" #6).
